[
    {
        "content": "<p>The following looks like a bug to me:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- this works:</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">37</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">37</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- but this does not:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: Tactic `rfl` failed: The left-hand side</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  n + m</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">is not definitionally equal to the right-hand side</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  42</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">m n : Nat</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">⊢ n + m = 42</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">37</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">42</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- `⊢ n + m = 42`</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- this also works:</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">37</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">42</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- `⊢ 37 + 5 = 42`</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Am I correct in assuming that <code>intro</code> is nowadays supposed to do what <code>rintro</code> does (thus making the latter obsolete)? (That <code>intro rfl</code> works as expected points in this direction, also, <code>intro ⟨h, h'⟩</code> works as expected.)</li>\n<li>If yes, then the above indicates a bug in <code>intro</code>.</li>\n<li>If no, then it is still a bug in <code>intro</code>, which then should raise an error rather than silently throwing away the introduced hypotheses.</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 606746727,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1782486244
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think <code>rintro</code> is obsolete. See below:</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">37</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- syntax error</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- `⊢ n + m = 42`</span>\n<span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True.intro</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- this also works:</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">37</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"n\">rintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- `⊢ n + m = 42`</span>\n<span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True.intro</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>",
        "id": 606763501,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1782490943
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So what iss the conclusion? I'd vote for fixing <code>intro</code> so that it has all the features of <code>rintro</code>. Or is there something relevant that the current <code>intro</code> does, but <code>rintro</code> does not?</p>",
        "id": 606772848,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1782494025
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What are/were the reasons for there being both <code>rintro</code> and <code>intro</code> in the first place?</p>",
        "id": 606789388,
        "sender_full_name": "Felix Pernegger",
        "timestamp": 1782499191
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Originally <code>intro</code> did not support pattern matching.</p>",
        "id": 606800416,
        "sender_full_name": "Etienne Marion",
        "timestamp": 1782503521
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Even now they support different kinds of pattern matching.</p>",
        "id": 606816550,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1782511298
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Since <code>intro</code> accepts arbitrary terms, it supports the syntax in the first example below, but as you can see, <code>rintro</code> requires different syntax.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">And</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hq</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 606818182,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1782512374
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- this works:</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">37</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">37</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"479359\">@Michael Stoll</span>, the reason this works is that the first <code>rfl</code> isn't the magic <code>rfl</code> keyword that <code>rintro</code> supports, it is rather the term <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=rfl#doc\">docs#rfl</a>.</p>",
        "id": 606818571,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1782512663
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Except that the reason the first one works is that the first <code>rfl</code> is the magic <code>rfl</code> that <code>intro</code> supports as explained in its documentation (on hover):</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>intro rfl</code> is short for <code>intro h; subst h</code>, if <code>h</code> is an equality where the left-hand or right-hand side is a variable.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Although I should clarify, <code>intro (rfl)</code> also works, but does something different, replacing <code>37</code> with <code>n</code>. That's why the second example doesn't work; it's trying to replace <code>37</code> with <code>n</code> and <code>5</code> with <code>m</code> and not the other way round.</p>",
        "id": 606820287,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1782514160
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the explanations.<br>\nHow often is the pattern matching feature of <code>intro</code> actually used (in Mathlib, say), and in these cases, could it be replaced by <code>rintro</code>? It is a bit confusing to have two similar, but slightly different, tactics that do more or less the same...</p>",
        "id": 606890644,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1782552874
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is one in core and one in mathlib?</p>",
        "id": 606908509,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1782569327
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>rintro</code> is in Init.RCases, which I assume is part of core.</p>",
        "id": 606909561,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1782570364
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note there’s also <code>intros</code> which does something slightly different from either</p>",
        "id": 606909967,
        "sender_full_name": "David Ang",
        "timestamp": 1782570753
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It used to be that <code>rintro</code> was in Mathlib (Mario wrote it), but it moved to core quite a while ago. The issue with merging them is that it would be a breaking change no matter which choices are made.</p>",
        "id": 606925539,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1782584461
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This feels like the sort of breaking change we should make, but needs a little bit more support tooling:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>so everyone gets code action / try this suggestions to do the migration \"one location at time\"</li>\n<li>there's (generic) tooling to apply all such suggestions at library scale.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>(I think we're closer than ever to having these things, but I've lost track of recent progress on this front.)</p>",
        "id": 606957745,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1782617458
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(psst, skimmer can currently do the second thing (available in mathlib under <code>scripts/runSkimmer.sh</code>), but it would be much less awkward and more robust if that sort of thing could be provided by core! :) )</p>",
        "id": 606961145,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1782620407
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Are there places where skimmer is deployed, e.g. in CI to fix deprecations? It would be nice to have working examples to crib from.</p>",
        "id": 606970256,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1782630845
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110087\">Kim Morrison</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/intro.20and.20rfl/near/606970256\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Are there places where skimmer is deployed, e.g. in CI to fix deprecations? It would be nice to have working examples to crib from.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>My understanding is \"no\". (For instance, deprecations don't generate \"try this\" suggestions right now. Yes, it would be really nice if this could get fixed.)</p>",
        "id": 606998238,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1782660935
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Lately I’ve backburnered skimmer to work on other projects, but hope to get back to it in a little while as those projects come to fruition and would love to make this happen :)</p>",
        "id": 607001719,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1782663979
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>No problem, I know there is an incredible amount going on here. Just nice to make sure the \"last 10%\" (i.e. last 90% in reality!) of getting things actually deployed happens. I am definitely failing at this at the moment on several projects...</p>",
        "id": 607036994,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1782693763
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110087\">Kim Morrison</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/intro.20and.20rfl/near/606957745\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This feels like the sort of breaking change we should make</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110087\">@Kim Morrison</span>  In which direction exactly? This issue has been discussed before; namely, <code>have</code>/<code>let</code> use the <code>intro</code>-style syntax, whereas <code>rintro</code>/<code>obtain</code> use the <code>rcases</code> pattern-style syntax.</p>",
        "id": 607175784,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1782746621
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If work on <code>rcases</code> patterns is on the docket at some point, I would still really like to have <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/named.20subgoals.20with.20.60obtain.60\">#mathlib4 &gt; named subgoals with &#96;obtain&#96;</a></p>",
        "id": 607177086,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1782746930
    }
]